lley Art Festival - showcasing over 140 murals in downtown Sioux City's alleys - and presents monthly visual art exhibits featuring local and regional artists.|basic_html|About Vangarde ArtsVangarde Arts is an intimate nonprofit arts venue that has become a cornerstone of Sioux City's cultural scene. Located in the heart of downtown - this venue seamlessly blends visual and performance arts in a welcoming atmosphere.The Venue ExperienceWith its compact yet well-outfitted space - Vangarde Arts features a gallery lounge and intimate listening room with acoustics that are second to none. The venue has clean facilities and a well-stocked bar - creating a comfortable environment for all visitors.Music ProgrammingBeyond the weekly open mic - Vangarde Arts hosts an impressive lineup of touring acts throughout the year. The venue has welcomed legendary musicians like Johnny Winter - John Primer - James McMurtry - and Patricia Barber - as well as rising stars in blues - jazz - rock - folk - and bluegrass. Most ticketed shows take place on Friday and Saturday nights - featuring both nationally acclaimed artists and local original bands.Community ImpactOpen Mic Thursdays have become a community staple - drawing aspiring musicians and supportive audiences. The venue also hosts the annual Alley Art Festival - showcasing over 140 murals in downtown Sioux City's alleys - and presents monthly visual art exhibits featuring local and regional artists.","42.495115490491|-96.403349097341||42.495115490491, -96.403349097341",,,"In Person from 7:00 PM",,908|node|5dc8d733-f86f-4a37-95df-22ae640f692e|/vangarde-arts,"Vangarde Arts",
