st opened in 1979 and has been called the CBGB of the South. After a five-year closure the venue triumphantly reopened in September 2025 reclaiming its spot as Miami's home for underground music art and culture.Music LegacyChurchill's holds the world record for most acts within a single venue having hosted over 20000 performances. Famous musicians including Marilyn Manson Social Distortion The Mavericks Dick Dale Agent Orange and Iggy Pop have all played the pub. The venue has shaped generations of artists and fostered Miami's untamed creative energy.Atmosphere and EventsKnown as the cradle of everything indie and the institution for live music in Miami Churchill's hosts events every night of the week. The venue features both an indoor stage and outdoor beer garden courtyard. Monday nights feature Jazz in the Church with the Fernando Ulibarri Quartet leading world-class improvisation while the Raven Open Mic unfolds in the Bohemian beer garden with spoken word poets musicians and visual artists.","25.826380221263|-80.191289550698||25.826380221263, -80.191289550698","Fernando Ulibarri Quartet",,"In Person",,742|node|4f1b2f1a-e385-4c74-b317-94df5988adf9|/churchills-pub,"Churchill's Pub",
