nue is walkable bikeable and has car parking available making it easily accessible from downtown Lincoln.|basic_html|About Hub CafeHub Cafe is a farmer-owned cafe that opened in 2016 at the scenic Jayne Snyder Trails Center in Lincoln's Telegraph District. The venue is rooted in community connections and sources sustainable foods from local growers and small farms in Lincoln and the surrounding area.Open Mic NightsThe Hub Cafe hosts open mic nights on the first and third Thursday of each month from 5-8pm with equipment setup sponsored by Roots Music. The events welcome musicians singers comedians and poets and always end with a large jam session. Chefs Jake and Kelley provide a rotating monthly menu of pizza and small bites to enjoy during performances.Other EventsThe venue also hosts Hub and Soul - a free community event featuring music local food and Lincoln's parks held on select dates throughout the summer months at nearby Union Plaza Amphitheatre. Friday nights feature live local music and creative pizzas making it a popular weekend destination in the Telegraph District.The SpaceLocated at the Jayne Snyder Trails Center the Hub Cafe offers a welcoming atmosphere with views overlooking the beautiful Antelope Valley. The venue is walkable bikeable and has car parking available making it easily accessible from downtown Lincoln.","40.816175546386|-96.689360793764||40.816175546386, -96.689360793764","Roots Music",,"In Person from 5:00 PM",,668|node|c1ca552b-9bd7-4a06-8b8f-cdb4c066f4c5|/hub-cafe,"Hub Cafe",
