 soulful pop and R&B style. Latin music plays throughout creating an energetic warm environment. The venue accepts credit cards offers bike and street parking and is open seven days a week with extended hours on weekends.|basic_html|About Mint to Be Mojito Bar and BitesMint to Be Mojito Bar and Bites is tucked away in a quiet corner of downtown Savannah at 12 W State St. This Latin-inspired establishment specializes in handcrafted mojitos and authentic Latin bites creating a vibrant welcoming atmosphere.Food and DrinkThe bar focuses specifically on the art of the perfect mojito with fresh fruit hand-muddled and made to order. Flavors include classic strawberry coconut passionfruit pineapple and seasonal varieties. Non-alcoholic mojitos are also available. The food menu showcases authentic Latin-inspired bites including empanadas arepas tamales papa rellenas and Cuban sandwiches all made with fresh quality ingredients.La Aparicion SpeakeasyBehind a hidden door accessed through the private bathroom is La Aparicion a secret speakeasy lounge. This upscale space features vibey decor an antique-trendy forest aesthetic and creative cocktails served with little lights for a fun experience. The speakeasy is available for private events and cocktail classes teaching Latin American craft cocktail techniques.Music and AtmosphereSunday evenings from 6-9 PM feature open mic hosted by Jacob Evans known for his soulful pop and R&B style. Latin music plays throughout creating an energetic warm environment. The venue accepts credit cards offers bike and street parking and is open seven days a week with extended hours on weekends.","32.078694244584|-81.092278022626||32.078694244584, -81.092278022626","Jacob Evans",,"In Person from 6:00 PM",,645|node|b2dbb677-2815-401c-b699-58b17527765c|/mint-be-mojito-bar-and-bites,"Mint to Be Mojito Bar and Bites",
652,500c3d3b-9a80-4a6f-9e1c-414acf81f5d9,672,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-02-22T23:06:03+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",0|user|be5374ea-047e-466c-bcb7-99c31dfe5df9|/user/0,,1,0|user|be5374ea-047e-466c-bcb7-99c31dfe5df9|/user/0,"Open Mic/Talent Showcase @ The Sentient Bean","2026-02-22T23:06:03+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-23T00:02:52+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Open Mic/Talent Showcase @ The Sentient Bean | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/open-mictalent-showcase-sentient-bean",/open-mictalent-showcase-sentient-bean|478|en,,,"1st and 3rd Tuesdays","Family-friendly open mic on 1st and 3rd Tuesdays welcoming poetry music singing drag and performance art. An anything-goes showcase emphasizing new original thoughtful work in an intimate listening room.",,"13 E Park Ave Savannah GA 31401","Sign up 6:30 PM Show 7:00 PM","About The Sentient BeanThe Sentient Bean is an independently owned cafe and vegetarian restaurant located directly across from Forsyth Park in the heart of Savannah. More than just a coffeehouse it's a gathering space dedicated to conscious consumption and community activism.Food and BeveragesThe cafe serves fair trade organic coffee and espresso drinks with a menu featuring organic and locally sourced ingredients often purchased directly from farmers. Homemade baked goods include whole wheat and gluten-free options. Sunday brunch runs from 9 AM to 12 PM. The venue has been voted Best Coffeehouse Best Vegetarian Restaurant Best Indie Film Venue and Best Green Business by Connect Savannah readers.Music and EventsMost evenings the dining room converts into an intimate listening room hosting live music open mics films and community forums. The space features vaulted 22-foot wood ceilings a modest 5x7 ft stage and can seat up to 50 people or accommodate 70 standing. The acoustics favor acoustic music but the venue welcomes diverse genres poetry comedy burlesque small-scale theater drag and film showings.Open Mic DetailsTongue open mouth and music night happens every 1st and 3rd Tuesday. Sign-up begins at 6:30 PM with the show starting at 7 PM. The event is free open to all and family-friendly emphasizing new original thoughtful work. Anything goes from poetry and music to singing drag and performance art making it a true community talent showcase.AtmosphereThe Sentient Bean buzzes with positive energy featuring eclectic decor high ceilings and an open layout that fosters creativity. Happy hour runs daily from 5-9 PM with $5 wine and $3 beer. The community-focused space attracts locals and visitors seeking a welcoming inclusive environment.|basic_html|About The Sentient BeanThe Sentient Bean is an independently owned cafe and vegetarian restaurant located directly across from Forsyth Park in the heart of Savannah. More than just a coffeehouse it's a gathering space dedicated to conscious consumption and community activism.Food and BeveragesThe cafe serves fair trade organic coffee and espresso drinks with a menu featuring organic and locally sourced ingredients often purchased directly from farmers. Homemade baked goods include whole wheat and gluten-free options. Sunday brunch runs from 9 AM to 12 PM. The venue has been voted Best Coffeehouse Best Vegetarian Restaurant Best Indie Film Venue and Best Green Business by Connect Savannah readers.Music and EventsMost evenings the dining room converts into an intimate listening room hosting live music open mics films and community forums. The space features vaulted 22-foot wood ceilings a modest 5x7 ft stage and can seat up to 50 people or accommodate 70 standing. The acoustics favor acoustic music but the venue welcomes diverse genres poetry comedy burlesque small-scale theater drag and film showings.Open Mic DetailsTongue open mouth and music night happens every 1st and 3rd Tuesday. Sign-up begins at 6:30 PM with the show starting at 7 PM. The event is free open to all and family-friendly emphasizing new original thoughtful work. Anything goes from poetry and music to singing drag and performance art making it a true community talent showcase.AtmosphereThe Sentient Bean buzzes with positive energy featuring eclectic decor high ceilings and an open layout that fosters creativity. Happy hour runs daily from 5-9 PM with $5 wine and $3 beer. The community-focused space attracts locals and visitors seeking a welcoming inclusive environment.","32.064791601143|-81.096304803577||32.064791601143, -81.096304803577",,,"In Person from 6:30 PM",,646|node|05db4dfd-c53e-4ac4-8f39-827c4c463220|/sentient-bean,"The Sentient Bean",
