ned as a breakfast café for produce dockworkers the venue was converted to a pub by the McMenamin brothers and has evolved into a beloved spot for craft beer and live music.Music and EventsThe venue hosts a diverse range of live music events including jazz sessions funk nights and DJ events. The Tuesday night jazz jam has become a Portland institution attracting both seasoned professionals and emerging talent. The café's basement-style venue creates an intimate casual atmosphere perfect for musical exploration.Amenities and AtmosphereProduce Row features a covered and heated patio multiple indoor spaces and a vast beer selection with over 20 taps and 200+ bottles. The Central Eastside Industrial District location provides easy access and ample street parking. The venue is known for its relaxed vibe and commitment to supporting local music.","45.520154107431|-122.662915241||45.520154107431, -122.662915241","Pablo Rivarola",,"In Person",,585|node|23b4d270-a0c9-4006-ad1d-4eda4613bda7|/produce-row-cafe,"Produce Row Café",
