uilding community by creating an environment that connects musicians of all abilities through live music. The studio is conveniently located near the intersection of Highway 26 and Highway 217 in Beaverton with easy TriMet access via Bus Line 20.Regular Jam SessionsCommunity Jams hosts multiple weekly jam sessions including Monday No Request Refused Jam Monday Improv Jam Thursday Themed Jams Saturday Newcomer/Explorer Jam and bi-monthly Blues and Acoustic Jams. Each session is designed to be welcoming to musicians of all skill levels.Mission and SupportThe organization receives support from Pearl Jam's Future Days Fund the Fred W. Fields fund of Oregon Community Foundation and the Marie Lamfrom Charitable Foundation. They are also supported by the Oregon Arts Commission. Donations help cover the $24 per person per jam operating costs.","45.503443772946|-122.80400268466||45.503443772946, -122.80400268466",Ben,,"RSVP required",https://communityjams.org,,"Community Jams Studio",
573,2ab3ca07-1e3f-4cd2-8f4a-af84ea280620,593,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-02-22T16:34:08+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",0|user|be5374ea-047e-466c-bcb7-99c31dfe5df9|/user/0,,1,0|user|be5374ea-047e-466c-bcb7-99c31dfe5df9|/user/0,"Jackson Hole Hootenanny @ Dornan's Spur Bar","2026-02-22T16:34:08+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-22T16:35:24+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Jackson Hole Hootenanny @ Dornan's Spur Bar | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/jackson-hole-hootenanny-dornans-spur-bar",/jackson-hole-hootenanny-dornans-spur-bar|404|en,"Acoustic instruments only",,Mondays,"Weekly acoustic open mic night featuring folk and traditional music in one of Jackson Hole's most iconic settings. Local and visiting musicians perform two-song sets against the backdrop of the Teton Range.",,"12170 Dornan Rd Moose WY 83012","5:00 PM - 8:30 PM","About Dornan'sDornan's is a family-owned establishment in Grand Teton National Park that has been serving the community since 1922. The venue offers breathtaking views of the Teton Range and sits along the Snake River in Moose Wyoming.The Hootenanny TraditionThe Jackson Hole Hootenanny began in the 1950s as informal jam sessions under the Snake River bridge led by legendary mountaineer Bill Briggs. After moving to Dornan's in the 1990s the event has become one of Jackson's most beloved musical traditions. During summer months the Hootenanny takes place outdoors at the Chuckwagon stage while winter sessions move to the Silver Dollar Bar at the Wort Hotel downtown.Other Events at Dornan'sBeyond the Hootenanny Dornan's hosts various community gatherings and offers year-round dining at their Pizza & Pasta Company. The venue features a Trading Post grocery store wine shop and seasonal outdoor Chuckwagon restaurant making it a complete destination within Grand Teton National Park.|basic_html|About Dornan'sDornan's is a family-owned establishment in Grand Teton National Park that has been serving the community since 1922. The venue offers breathtaking views of the Teton Range and sits along the Snake River in Moose Wyoming.The Hootenanny TraditionThe Jackson Hole Hootenanny began in the 1950s as informal jam sessions under the Snake River bridge led by legendary mountaineer Bill Briggs. After moving to Dornan's in the 1990s the event has become one of Jackson's most beloved musical traditions. During summer months the Hootenanny takes place outdoors at the Chuckwagon stage while winter sessions move to the Silver Dollar Bar at the Wort Hotel downtown.Other Events at Dornan'sBeyond the Hootenanny Dornan's hosts various community gatherings and offers year-round dining at their Pizza & Pasta Company. The venue features a Trading Post grocery store wine shop and seasonal outdoor Chuckwagon restaurant making it a complete destination within Grand Teton National Park.","43.657668488536|-110.71028899842||43.657668488536, -110.71028899842","John Sidle and rotating hosts",,"In Person from 5:00 PM",,567|node|5984ae4f-88c1-4757-8663-611b11bca409|/dornans-spur-bar,"Dornan's Spur Bar",
