a. This down-to-earth live music venue in St. Paul's Payne-Phalen neighborhood has a capacity of 360 people and specializes in blues - R&B - and rock shows.Open Stage EventsThe Twin Cities' only Open Stage and Cool Stuff Bazaar takes place on the first Wednesday of each month from 6-9 PM. Musicians can join in with the house band - perform solo - or bring their own band. The event is acoustic-oriented but welcomes all styles. Artists - crafters - creators - and flea marketers are invited to bring their creations to display and sell.Venue AtmosphereThe venue features a full bar - pub fare - and an intimate atmosphere perfect for experiencing live music up close. The cafe regularly hosts blues - R&B - rock - and roots music performances. With great sound quality and a welcoming environment - Minnesota Music Cafe has become a beloved fixture in St. Paul's music scene.","44.956508493019|-93.077711500671||44.956508493019, -93.077711500671","Rotating Hosts",,"In Person",,476|node|80961413-a3db-486d-9a34-a45b564393c1|/minnesota-music-cafe,"Minnesota Music Cafe",
