age architecture creates interesting sight lines throughout the space.|basic_html|Fox & Goose Public HouseHistoric English-Style Pub and Music VenueLocated within the Fuller Building and opened in 1975 - Fox & Goose has become a Sacramento institution. This authentic English-style pub serves breakfast - lunch - and dinner alongside a carefully curated selection of wines - beers - and cocktails. The building itself dates to 1913 and maintains an old-factory-brick aesthetic that adds character to every performance.Live Music ProgrammingThe venue hosts live music five nights per week - anchored by Monday's legendary open mic night that has run continuously for over 30 years. Weekend performances feature varied bands across multiple genres. Tuesday evenings feature Pub Quiz trivia night - creating a full week of community engagement and entertainment.Dining and AtmosphereThe pub serves traditional English fare including fish and chips - bangers and mash - and olallieberry scones for breakfast alongside American classics. The intimate layout creates a warm - welcoming atmosphere where regulars and newcomers alike feel at home. Many seats face the performance area - though the vintage architecture creates interesting sight lines throughout the space.","38.571723481646|-121.4961805724||38.571723481646, -121.4961805724","Dave Baldwin",,"In Person from 6:30 PM",,437|node|6882496b-9779-4bcc-a77a-0e2ba25a62ad|/fox-goose-public-house,"Fox & Goose Public House",
