lian influenced home-style cooking. The building's 88-year history is evident in every corner - creating an authentic Sacramento experience.|basic_html|Old IronsidesSacramento's Historic Music VenueEstablished in 1934 with the first liquor license issued in Sacramento County after Prohibition - Old Ironsides holds the distinction of being Sacramento's oldest continuously operating bar. The family-owned establishment has evolved from a neighborhood watering hole for politicians into one of the city's premier small-scale music venues - with a capacity of 150 people.Live Music HeritageOld Ironsides hosts live music Thursday through Saturday nights - featuring local and touring acts across rock - indie - punk - and alternative genres. The venue gained legendary status in the 1990s when the next generation of the Kanelos family transformed it into a nightclub. Wednesday night open mics have become a staple - while the LIPSTICK indie rock dance party has run monthly for over 20 years - drawing lines around the building.Venue CharacterThe intimate brick-walled space features excellent acoustics and a stage in the adjoining showroom. The venue maintains its dive bar charm while providing professional sound quality. Tuesday nights feature karaoke - and the venue previously served lunch with Greek and Italian influenced home-style cooking. The building's 88-year history is evident in every corner - creating an authentic Sacramento experience.","38.570396406459|-121.4971471582||38.570396406459, -121.4971471582",,,"In Person from 8:30 PM",,438|node|c5dbcc28-6ab6-4e30-96ab-9e1b0d73ae05|/old-ironsides,"Old Ironsides",
