347,4cf440ec-4e54-4fe3-8761-1887bda534b8,365,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-02-21T20:34:22+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Open Mic @ Brothers Lounge - Front Stage","2026-02-21T20:30:25+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-21T20:34:22+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Open Mic @ Brothers Lounge - Front Stage | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/open-mic-brothers-lounge",/open-mic-brothers-lounge|188|en,"Full Backline",,Wednesdays,"Every Wednesday at Brothers Lounge, the newly christened Front Stage comes alive with Cleveland's emerging talent. Hosted by multi-instrumentalist singer-songwriter Connor Mancini (who performs as Moon Cactus)",,"11609 Detroit Ave, Cleveland, OH 44102","8:00 PM start","The VibeBrothers Lounge embodies Cleveland's classic live music venue spirit across its three distinct spaces—a neighborhood pub, the Front Stage (formerly an intimate wine bar), and the 350-capacity concert hall. The Front Stage, with room for about 80 patrons, provides an intimate setting where the focus stays on the music. It's a space where students, seasoned players, and everyone in between can showcase their talents without pretense.The PerformancesSign-ups begin at 7:30 PM with performances starting at 8:00 PM. The venue welcomes all genres—from folk to punk to metal—reflecting host Moon Cactus's eclectic musical background (""anti-pop"" as he calls it). With full backline available and its own bar, performers have everything they need to deliver quality performances.The 80-cent wing special makes it easy to make an evening of it, whether you're performing or supporting fellow musicians. The no-cover-charge policy keeps the barrier to entry low, and the supportive atmosphere created by regular attendees helps emerging artists build confidence.This Wednesday tradition represents Brothers Lounge's commitment to being more than just a concert venue—it's a true musical community hub where local talent can develop their craft and potentially graduate to the larger concert hall stage.|basic_html|The VibeBrothers Lounge embodies Cleveland's classic live music venue spirit across its three distinct spaces—a neighborhood pub, the Front Stage (formerly an intimate wine bar), and the 350-capacity concert hall. The Front Stage, with room for about 80 patrons, provides an intimate setting where the focus stays on the music. It's a space where students, seasoned players, and everyone in between can showcase their talents without pretense.The PerformancesSign-ups begin at 7:30 PM with performances starting at 8:00 PM. The venue welcomes all genres—from folk to punk to metal—reflecting host Moon Cactus's eclectic musical background (""anti-pop"" as he calls it). With full backline available and its own bar, performers have everything they need to deliver quality performances.The 80-cent wing special makes it easy to make an evening of it, whether you're performing or supporting fellow musicians. The no-cover-charge policy keeps the barrier to entry low, and the supportive atmosphere created by regular attendees helps emerging artists build confidence.This Wednesday tradition represents Brothers Lounge's commitment to being more than just a concert venue—it's a true musical community hub where local talent can develop their craft and potentially graduate to the larger concert hall stage.","41.483442737397|-81.765555829076||41.483442737397, -81.765555829076","Moon Cactus (Connor Mancini)",,"In Person - 7:30PM",,,"Brothers Lounge",
345,3fb44d79-630e-41ce-9145-5b13aa13e298,363,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-02-21T20:24:09+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"BOP STOP @ The Music Settlement","2026-02-21T20:19:44+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-21T20:27:51+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|BOP STOP @ The Music Settlement | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/bop-stop-the-music-settlement",/bop-stop-the-music-settlement|186|en,"Yes - professional backline",,"Weekly on Fridays","BOP STOP stands as Cleveland's premier listening room—an intimate, acoustically pristine performance venue with sweeping views of Lake Erie. Donated to The Music Settlement in late 2013, this West Side gem has become one of the most respected jazz venues",,"2920 Detroit Ave, Cleveland, OH 44113",Varies,"Jazz Jam Session at BOP STOPEvery Friday evening, Cleveland's premier jazz listening room hosts one of the city's most respected jam sessions. Led by talented local drummers Anthony Taddeo and trumpeter Garrett Folger (who alternate hosting duties), the BOP STOP Jazz Jam welcomes players of all skill levels to sit in with a professional house rhythm section.The VibeThe atmosphere strikes a perfect balance between serious musicianship and welcoming inclusivity. BOP STOP's intimate, acoustically pristine space features tiered seating and sweeping views of Lake Erie, creating an environment where music is treated with reverence. The venue's ""quiet policy"" during performances ensures that musicians receive the focused attention their work deserves, while the all-ages policy and free admission (donations encouraged) make jazz accessible to everyone.The PerformancesMusicians bring their instruments and call tunes from the standard jazz repertoire—bebop classics, hard bop standards, contemporary compositions. The house rhythm section provides deep-in-the-pocket support that allows horn players, pianists, and vocalists to truly stretch out and explore. Whether you're a conservatory student testing classroom skills against real-time demands, a weekend warrior looking to blow off steam, or a seasoned professional stopping by between gigs, you'll find supportive colleagues and an audience that actually listens.The jam sessions are great for performers of all skill levels and listeners alike, embodying BOP STOP's mission to make world-class jazz experiences accessible to the entire Cleveland community.|basic_html|Jazz Jam Session at BOP STOPEvery Friday evening, Cleveland's premier jazz listening room hosts one of the city's most respected jam sessions. Led by talented local drummers Anthony Taddeo and trumpeter Garrett Folger (who alternate hosting duties), the BOP STOP Jazz Jam welcomes players of all skill levels to sit in with a professional house rhythm section.The VibeThe atmosphere strikes a perfect balance between serious musicianship and welcoming inclusivity. BOP STOP's intimate, acoustically pristine space features tiered seating and sweeping views of Lake Erie, creating an environment where music is treated with reverence. The venue's ""quiet policy"" during performances ensures that musicians receive the focused attention their work deserves, while the all-ages policy and free admission (donations encouraged) make jazz accessible to everyone.The PerformancesMusicians bring their instruments and call tunes from the standard jazz repertoire—bebop classics, hard bop standards, contemporary compositions. The house rhythm section provides deep-in-the-pocket support that allows horn players, pianists, and vocalists to truly stretch out and explore. Whether you're a conservatory student testing classroom skills against real-time demands, a weekend warrior looking to blow off steam, or a seasoned professional stopping by between gigs, you'll find supportive colleagues and an audience that actually listens.The jam sessions are great for performers of all skill levels and listeners alike, embodying BOP STOP's mission to make world-class jazz experiences accessible to the entire Cleveland community.","41.490066851312|-81.71110180469||41.490066851312, -81.71110180469",,,"In Person",,346|node|70e8f490-6e11-4736-9d94-f8b3afec8942|/the-music-settlement-cleveland-oh,"The Music Settlement",
