266,d88a9da1-2494-4aec-99f0-266ae4397cfc,282,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-02-17T03:54:47+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Cafe Nine Saturday Afternoon Jazz Jam","2026-02-17T03:46:05+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-17T03:54:47+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Cafe Nine Saturday Afternoon Jazz Jam | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/cafe-nine-saturday-jazz-jam",/cafe-nine-saturday-jazz-jam|150|en,"Full Back Line",,Saturdays,"Saturday afternoon Jazz jam to kick the weekend off and get you in the groove",,"250 State St, New Haven, CT 06510","4PM - 7PM","New Haven's Longest-Running Jazz TraditionFor over 20 years, Cafe Nine's Saturday afternoon jazz jam has been a cornerstone of New Haven's music scene. Every Saturday from 4:00 to 7:00 PM, this intimate venue becomes a gathering place for jazz musicians and enthusiasts seeking authentic musical communion.The VibeHosted by rotating house bands—often featuring ""Dr. G"" Gary Grippo on guitar, Jeff Fuller on bass, and Barry Ries on drums and trumpet—the jam maintains a welcoming yet musically serious atmosphere. This is straight-ahead jazz played with skill and passion, where musicians respect the tradition while bringing their own voices to classic standards and bebop tunes.The afternoon time slot creates a unique energy. Unlike late-night jazz clubs, the Saturday jam attracts families, students, and working musicians who appreciate daytime jamming. Natural light filters through the historic venue as music fills the room, creating an atmosphere that feels both casual and focused.The PerformancesThe format follows traditional jazz jam etiquette: the house band opens with a set establishing the vibe and demonstrating the musical level, then invites participating musicians to sit in. Bring your instrument, listen to the first set, and join the rotation. The house rhythm section provides solid, professional support that allows horn players, guitarists, pianists, and vocalists to stretch out and explore.Musicians appreciate the supportive audience—people who actually came for the music, not just to drink. The sound quality is excellent for a venue this size, and the stage setup puts performers in direct connection with listeners. No cover charge means accessibility for everyone, whether performing or listening.The jam attracts a mix of conservatory students from Yale and other regional music programs, veteran players maintaining their chops, and emerging musicians developing their jazz vocabulary. Expect to hear bebop standards, hard bop classics, and contemporary jazz compositions played with genuine feeling and technical skill.New Haven Jazz Underground Tuesday Jam at Cafe NineGrassroots Jazz Community BuildingOn the 2nd and 4th Tuesday of each month, Cafe Nine hosts the New Haven Jazz Underground's jam session, providing a different flavor than the Saturday afternoon gathering. Running from 7:00 to 9:00 PM, this bi-weekly event represents grassroots community organizing around jazz music.The VibeThe New Haven Jazz Underground operates as a community-based organization dedicated to promoting jazz in all its forms. Their Tuesday jams feature a house band or featured performer followed by an open jam session where musicians can participate. The evening time slot attracts a slightly different crowd than the weekend afternoon—more working professionals unwinding after the workday, students between evening classes, and dedicated jazz heads seeking midweek musical connection.The format emphasizes accessibility and community building. There's no cover charge, no pressure to purchase drinks or food, just a welcoming space for jazz to happen. The organization's commitment to supporting all forms of jazz means you might hear traditional standards alongside more experimental approaches, creating a broader musical palette than strictly bebop-focused jams.The PerformancesPerformances begin with a featured artist or house band establishing the evening's direction. This might be a local player showcasing their trio, a visiting musician sitting in with New Haven players, or a collaborative project bringing together musicians from different scenes. After the opening set, the jam opens to all participants.The supportive atmosphere encourages musicians at various skill levels to participate. Experienced players mentor emerging musicians, sharing knowledge about changes, suggesting tunes, and creating space for musical growth. It's jazz as community practice rather than competitive proving ground.The intimate Cafe Nine setting creates direct connection between performers and audience. Unlike large jazz clubs where performers feel distant, here you're part of the same room, sharing the same experience. Conversations between sets build relationships and networks that sustain New Haven's jazz ecology.|basic_html|New Haven's Longest-Running Jazz TraditionFor over 20 years, Cafe Nine's Saturday afternoon jazz jam has been a cornerstone of New Haven's music scene. Every Saturday from 4:00 to 7:00 PM, this intimate venue becomes a gathering place for jazz musicians and enthusiasts seeking authentic musical communion.The VibeHosted by rotating house bands—often featuring ""Dr. G"" Gary Grippo on guitar, Jeff Fuller on bass, and Barry Ries on drums and trumpet—the jam maintains a welcoming yet musically serious atmosphere. This is straight-ahead jazz played with skill and passion, where musicians respect the tradition while bringing their own voices to classic standards and bebop tunes.The afternoon time slot creates a unique energy. Unlike late-night jazz clubs, the Saturday jam attracts families, students, and working musicians who appreciate daytime jamming. Natural light filters through the historic venue as music fills the room, creating an atmosphere that feels both casual and focused.The P