263,caa82db9-9e94-4773-b234-1c0fc24b8a21,279,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-02-10T18:33:45+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",2|user|7c138690-61ff-421c-9151-b6f0e3d92409|/user/2,,1,2|user|7c138690-61ff-421c-9151-b6f0e3d92409|/user/2,"Esmeralda's Acoustic Open Mic Night","2026-02-10T18:33:45+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-15T14:56:29+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Esmeralda's Acoustic Open Mic Night | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/node/263",en,"None - Acoustic Open Mic",esmeraldasopenmic@gmail.com,"Every Second and Fourth Friday of the Month","Acoustic Open Mic Night Every Second and Forrth Friday of the Month","26|Bimonthly Acoustic Open Mic||1200|900|file|ad01b821-5e75-4c6d-9728-48254c0fb789|https://openjamevents.com/sites/default/files/2026-02/2026%20February%20Dates.png","1515 North Point Drive #108 Durham, NC",6:30,"Durham’s vibrant cultural scene just gained a fresh new voice. Esmeralda's Cafe, long celebrated as a local haven for exquisite coffee and authentic Latin-inspired fare, has recently opened its doors to the performing arts with the introduction of a new, bi-weekly Open Mic Night. This initiative transforms the cozy coffeehouse into a stage for the community, promising a new cornerstone for local talent.Held every other Friday, the event is quickly becoming a beacon for artists—musicians, poets, storytellers, and comedians—looking for a welcoming platform to share their work. It's a perfect synergy: the relaxed atmosphere of a coffee shop meets the electric energy of live performance.|basic_html|Durham’s vibrant cultural scene just gained a fresh new voice. Esmeralda's Cafe, long celebrated as a local haven for exquisite coffee and authentic Latin-inspired fare, has recently opened its doors to the performing arts with the introduction of a new, bi-weekly Open Mic Night. This initiative transforms the cozy coffeehouse into a stage for the community, promising a new cornerstone for local talent.Held every other Friday, the event is quickly becoming a beacon for artists—musicians, poets, storytellers, and comedians—looking for a welcoming platform to share their work. It's a perfect synergy: the relaxed atmosphere of a coffee shop meets the electric energy of live performance.","36.027665366745|-78.914723194952||36.027665366745, -78.914723194952",JoeSeph,,6:30,,6|node|7f58d109-df50-4dd8-bb73-6cb3e7b97d38|/node/6,"Esmeralda's Cafe",
255,adbd15d2-026a-46cf-a97b-a2f74656229f,271,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-02-04T21:17:56+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Open Mic @ Fox & Locke (Franklin)","2026-02-04T21:14:03+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-04T21:58:07+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Open Mic @ Fox & Locke (Franklin) | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/open-mic-fox-and-locke-franklin-tn",/open-mic-fox-and-locke-franklin-tn|140|en,,,Thursdays,"Open mic allowing both covers and originals",,"4142 Old Hillsboro Rd, Franklin, TN 37064","6PM Until","Open Mic Thursday at Fox & Locke (Franklin)Every Thursday evening, Fox & Locke in Leipers Fork (about 40 minutes southwest of Nashville) hosts an open mic that's become legendary in Middle Tennessee's music community. Unlike many Nashville open mics focused exclusively on original material, Fox & Locke welcomes both originals and covers, creating accessible, joyful celebration of music in all forms.The Vibe: Leipers Fork is a small community in Franklin, Tennessee, often called ""Nashville's Big Backyard."" The rural setting provides escape from the city's intensity while maintaining proximity to Music City's music community. Fox & Locke operates as restaurant and gathering space, offering full food and bar service alongside weekly music programming.Thursday nights have developed devoted following among musicians and music lovers willing to make the drive from Nashville. The atmosphere is described as ""unlike any other open mic you've been to""—welcoming, multigenerational, enthusiastic, and occasionally graced by surprise appearances from established artists who live in the area or are passing through.The venue's location in Leipers Fork attracts different demographic than urban Nashville open mics. Families with children, rural music lovers, and people seeking community connection show up alongside serious musicians. The result is audience that's genuinely enthusiastic rather than jaded or overly critical.Sign-ups start at 5:30 PM, and performers often arrive early to choose their preferred slot in the lineup. This competitive enthusiasm speaks to the event's popularity—people want to play here because the audience genuinely cares about the music.Performances: The open mic runs from 6 PM onward with each performer getting two songs. The acceptance of both original material and covers distinguishes this from many Nashville venues. You can test your original songs or simply share your interpretation of classics—both are valued equally.The ""occasional visit"" from established artists adds excitement and unpredictability. The Leipers Fork area attracts musicians who want to live outside Nashville's urban core, and some stop by Fox & Locke on Thursday nights to play informally. This creates magical moments when emerging performers share the stage with touring professionals.All ages are welcome, making this truly family-friendly event. Young musicians can perform alongside experienced players, children can watch performances, and the whole community can gather around music. This multigenerational approach keeps traditions alive while allowing innovation.The venue provides PA system and sound support—performers bring their instruments. The restaurant serves full menu, so attendees can make an evening of it with dinner and drinks alongside the music.For musicians willing to make the drive to Leipers Fork, Fox & Locke offers something increasingly rare: an open mic where the joy of music-making takes precedence over industry networking or competitive showcasing. The Thursday night gathering celebrates music as community-building art form, accessible to all and enjoyed by everyone.The rural setting, welcoming atmosphere, acceptance of covers, and genuine enthusiasm make Fox & Locke's Thursday open mic a beloved institution in Middle Tennessee'