alls.The session welcomes blues, jazz, R&B, funk, and soul musicians. Whether you play blues guitar, jazz saxophone, sing soul vocals, or hold down the pocket on bass, there's space for you. The house band provides solid support, and the rotating lineup ensures fresh energy each month.Musicians perform for free (no cover at the door for jam night), making Westside's exceptional facilities accessible to the community. The venue serves full bar service and often has food trucks on-site, creating a complete night-out experience.For West Valley musicians, this monthly session provides something rare: professional-level equipment and acoustics without the pressure of a ticketed show, in a venue that takes blues and jazz seriously.|basic_html|Westside Monthly Jam at Westside Blues, Jazz & MoreOn the first Thursday of every month, Westside Blues, Jazz & More opens its stage to the local music community for a jam session that's become one of the most popular nights at this Glendale venue. The monthly jam provides West Valley musicians access to professional equipment and an audience that genuinely appreciates blues and jazz.The Vibe: Westside Blues, Jazz & More was built as a temple to blues and jazz music—a Chicago-style speakeasy atmosphere with Prohibition-era décor, plush Chesterfield seating, exposed brick, and professional-grade acoustics. The venue operates Thursday through Sunday with ticketed shows featuring local legends and touring artists, but the monthly jam session is open to all.The crowd includes dedicated blues and jazz fans who make Westside their regular spot, West Valley residents who appreciate having world-class music in their neighborhood, and musicians from across the metro area who've heard about the quality of the room and equipment.Performances: The jam kicks off at 7:30 PM with a house band establishing the groove before opening to any musicians who wish to perform. The venue provides a complete professional backline—drums, bass amp, guitar amps,