 horn players, vocalists, and other instrumentalists who sit in.The session attracts accomplished jazz musicians from across the Valley—conservatory students, working professionals, touring musicians passing through town, and dedicated amateurs who've been studying the music for years. The house band knows hundreds of standards and can comp dynamically through complex changes, creating space for meaningful improvisation.Entry is $2 for performers and $5 for listeners—a token amount that makes The Nash's exceptional facilities and equipment accessible to the community. The bar serves beer, wine, and cocktails (BYOB also permitted), with food available from nearby restaurants.For jazz musicians, playing at The Nash—even during a jam session—represents a significant achievement. This is where serious students of the music can test their skills with top-tier accompaniment in a venue that's hosted jazz legends and continues to bring world-class artists to Phoenix.|basic_html|Sunday Jazz Jam at The Nash Jazz ClubEvery Sunday evening at The Nash Jazz Club transforms into one of the Valley's premier jazz jam sessions, led by acclaimed pianist Dave Henning. This weekly gathering represents the pinnacle of Phoenix's jazz scene accessibility—a chance to play with professional musicians in a world-class venue that's been named one of the top jazz clubs in America by DownBeat magazine.The Vibe: The Nash operates as a nonprofit with a mission to celebrate and preserve jazz through live performances and education. The 114-capacity venue feels intimate yet professional, with excellent acoustics designed specifically for jazz listening. The club maintains a ""quiet policy"" during performances, creating an environment where music receives the reverence it deserves.Sunday evenings have a more relaxed energy than ticketed shows—this is the jazz community coming together to play, learn, and share. The atmosphere balances serious musicianship with warmth and inclusivity.Performances: The jam runs from 6-9 PM, providing three hours for musicians to work through standards, bebop classics, and contemporary jazz compositions. Dave Henning leads a house rhythm section (piano, bass, drums) that provides professional-grade support for horn players, vocalists, and other instrumentalists who sit in.The session attracts accomplished jazz musicians from across the Valley—conservatory students, working professionals, touring musicians passing through town, and dedicated amateurs who've been studying the music for years. The house band knows hundreds of standards and can comp dynamically through complex changes, creating space for meaningful improvisation.Entry is $2 for performers and $5 for listeners—a token amount that makes The Nash's exceptional facilities and equipment accessible to the community. The bar serves beer, wine, and cocktails (BYOB also permitted), with food available from nearby restaurants.For jazz musicians, playing at The Nash—even during a jam session—represents a significant achievement. This is where serious students of the music can test their skills with top-tier accompaniment in a venue that's hosted jazz legends and continues to bring world-class artists to Phoenix.","33.459129180173|-112.07095170894||33.459129180173, -112.07095170894","Dave Henning",,,,,"The Nash Jazz Club",
235,14a079c3-d16e-4d4b-8f52-ce4ca47a215c,250,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-02-03T04:11:06+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Open Mic Monday @ Yucca Tap Room","2026-02-03T04:06:04+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-17T21:55:30+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Open Mic Monday @ Yucca Tap Room | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/yucca-tap-room-tempe-az",/yucca-tap-room-tempe-az|121|en,,,Mondays,"Acoustic open mic, 2 amps limit, Bring your own instruments",,"29 W Southern Ave, Tempe AZ 85282","8:00 PM - 11:00 PM","One of Arizona's longest-standing open mics happens every Monday night at Yucca Tap Room, Tempe's original live music venue that's been showcasing talent since the 1970s. This legendary dive bar has become an institution in the East Valley music scene, and Monday nights exemplify why.The VibeYucca Tap Room doesn't pretend to be anything it's not. This is a classic dive bar with cheap drinks, a no-bullshit atmosphere, and genuine appreciation for live music. The venue features Electric Bat Arcade on one side, adding pinball machines and vintage games to the mix. The crowd is eclectic—ASU students, longtime Tempe residents, musicians supporting their peers, and music lovers who've been coming here for decades.Performances Hosted by Kevin Redlich, the open mic welcomes acoustic acts primarily, though limited electric setups are allowed (maximum 2 amps, cocktail drum kits and cajons acceptable). Sign-ups begin at 8 PM with music starting at 9 PM. Each performer gets 3 songs or up to 15 minutes, giving everyone a fair shot at stage time.The talent level varies wonderfully—from first-timers nervously working through their original songs to seasoned musicians testing new material. The supportive audience creates an environment where taking creative risks feels safe. There's never a cover charge, and weekly drink specials make it accessible for broke musicians and budget-conscious music fans alike.The open mic draws singer-songwriters, folk musicians, acoustic rock acts, and everything in between. What makes Monday nights special is the longevity—this isn't some flash-in-the-pan event but a deeply rooted tradition that's helped launch countless local music careers while providing a consistent home for the Tempe music community. |basic_html|One of Arizona's longest-standing open mics happens every Monday night at Yucca Tap Room, Tempe's original live music venue that's been showcasing talent since the 1970s. This legendary dive bar has become an institution in the East Valley music scene, and Monday nights exemplify why.The VibeYucca Tap Room doesn't pretend to be anything it's not. This is a classic dive bar with cheap drinks, a no-bullshit atmosphere, and genuine appreciation for live music. The venue features Electric Bat Arcade on one side, adding pinball machines and vintage games to the mix. The crowd is eclectic—ASU students, longtime Tempe residents, musicians supporting their peers, and music lovers who've been coming here for decades.Performances Hosted by Kevin Redlich, the open mic welcomes acoustic acts primarily, though limited electric setups are allowed (maximum 2 amps, cocktail drum kits and cajons acceptable). Sign-ups begin at 8 PM with music starting at 9 PM. Each performer gets 3 songs or up to 15 minutes, giving everyone a fair shot at stage time.The talent level varies wonderfully—from first-timers nervously working through their original songs to seasoned musicians testing new material. The supportive audience creates an environment where taking creative risks feels safe. There's never a cover charge, and weekly drink specials make it accessible for broke musicians and budget-conscious music fans alike.The open mic draws singer-songwriters, folk musicians, acoustic rock acts, and everything in between. What makes Monday nights special is the longevity—this isn't some flash-in-the-pan event but a deeply rooted tradition that's helped launch countless local music careers while providing a consistent home for the Tempe music community. ","33.392827275033|-111.9405375||33.392827275033, -111.9405375","Kevin Redlich",,,,236|node|d1f30b85-45a7-46de-9a2b-1fe99609e064|/open-mic-yucca-tap-room,"Yucca Tap Room",
