141,f5e9ecb4-5adb-4c41-a317-908446301cd5,153,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-01-26T23:43:17+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Open Mic @ The Residency","2026-01-26T23:37:51+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-17T21:55:30+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Open Mic @ The Residency | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/open-mic-the-residency",/open-mic-the-residency|111|en,,,"3rd Wednesday Monthly","Chill open mic",,,"7:00 PM - 10:00 PM","The Residency - The Yard Private Social ClubEvery third Wednesday of the month, The Yard Private Social Club on South Orange Avenue hosts ""The Residency,"" a multidisciplinary showcase bringing together poets, artists, musicians, singers, dancers, painters, and writers for an evening of creative expression.The VibeThe Residency creates space for artistic community in South Orange's vibrant neighborhood scene. Host Craig Bradley curates an evening that blends spoken word, live music, visual art, and performance into a cohesive celebration of Newark's creative spirit. The social club setting provides an intimate, welcoming environment where artists can take risks and audiences can engage closely with the work.Running from 7:00 to 10:00 PM, the free event draws creative minds from across Newark and beyond. The atmosphere is supportive and inclusive, emphasizing artistic exploration over polished perfection. This is where emerging artists test new material, established artists try different mediums, and community gathers to witness creativity in action.PerformancesThe Residency welcomes all forms of artistic expression. Poets share verses, musicians perform original compositions or covers, dancers move, visual artists may present work—the format remains open and fluid. The event operates on the principle that artistic community thrives when boundaries between disciplines dissolve and creators support each other across mediums.The monthly frequency ensures a committed core community while remaining accessible to first-timers. Whether you're sharing your first public poem, debuting a new song, or simply soaking in Newark's creative energy, The Residency provides the space and audience to make it meaningful.|basic_html|The Residency - The Yard Private Social ClubEvery third Wednesday of the month, The Yard Private Social Club on South Orange Avenue hosts ""The Residency,"" a multidisciplinary showcase bringing together poets, artists, musicians, singers, dancers, painters, and writers for an evening of creative expression.The VibeThe Residency creates space for artistic community in South Orange's vibrant neighborhood scene. Host Craig Bradley curates an evening that blends spoken word, live music, visual art, and performance into a cohesive celebration of Newark's creative spirit. The social club setting provides an intimate, welcoming environment where artists can take risks and audiences can engage closely with the work.Running from 7:00 to 10:00 PM, the free event draws creative minds from across Newark and beyond. The atmosphere is supportive and inclusive, emphasizing artistic exploration over polished perfection. This is where emerging artists test new material, established artists try different mediums, and community gathers to witness creativity in action.PerformancesThe Residency welcomes all forms of artistic expression. Poets share verses, musicians perform original compositions or covers, dancers move, visual artists may present work—the format remains open and fluid. The event operates on the principle that artistic community thrives when boundaries between disciplines dissolve and creators support each other across mediums.The monthly frequency ensures a committed core community while remaining accessible to first-timers. Whether you're sharing your first public poem, debuting a new song, or simply soaking in Newark's creative energy, The Residency provides the space and audience to make it meaningful.",,"Craig Bradley",,"In Person",,,"The Residency - The Yard Private Social Club",
138,a2ec0559-a7f8-4da2-bfef-252388a1f1eb,150,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-01-26T23:28:52+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Jazz Jam @ Clement's Place","2026-01-26T23:23:33+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-17T21:55:30+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Jazz Jam @ Clement's Place | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/jazz-jam-clements-place",/jazz-jam-clements-place|108|en,"Full backline",,"Varies Monthly","Open Jazz Jam - Contact venue for dates and times",,"15 Washington St, Newark, NJ 07102","7:30 PM - 10:00 PM","Jazz Jam Sessions - Clement's PlaceCo-presented by NJPAC's Jazz Advisory Committee and Rutgers University-Newark's Institute of Jazz Studies, the monthly jazz jam sessions at Clement's Place honor the legacy of Dr. Clement A. Price, Newark's city historian and devoted jazz fan. This free monthly gathering attracts top-flight New Jersey musicians and welcomes jazz artists of all levels.The VibeClement's Place is a hidden gem—a cozy jazz club tucked inside a historic neo-classical building at 15 Washington Street, just steps from the Newark Museum. The venue operates as a cabaret-style space curated by Gregory Burrus Productions, bringing world-class jazz to an intimate downtown setting.The jam sessions feature a professional house band directed by pianist and bandleader James Austin Jr., providing the kind of solid musical foundation that allows horn players, vocalists, and instrumentalists to truly stretch out. The vibe honors Newark's deep jazz heritage (Sarah Vaughan, Wayne Shorter, James Moody) while remaining accessible to developing players.PerformancesAll novice and seasoned jazz musicians and singers are welcome to jam and improvise with the professional band throughout the night. The sessions run from 7:30 PM and create space for both serious jazz study and pure enjoyment of the music. With a full bar and an atmosphere that evokes classic jazz club intimacy, Clement's Place offers what many jam sessions can't: professional-grade backline, knowledgeable audiences, and a venue designed specifically for jazz listening.Registration is required but admission remains free, democratizing access to one of the region's finest jazz environments. These sessions move fast—bring your chops, your ears, and your willingness to engage with Newark's living jazz tradition.|basic_html|Jazz Jam Sessions - Clement's PlaceCo-presented by NJPAC's Jazz Advisory Committee and Rutgers University-Newark's Institute of Jazz Studies, the monthly jazz jam sessions at Clement's Place honor the legacy of Dr. Clement A. Price, Newark's city historian and devoted jazz fan. This free monthly gathering attracts top-flight New Jersey musicians and welcomes jazz artists of all levels.The VibeClement's Place is a hidden gem—a cozy jazz club tucked inside a historic neo-classical building at 15 Washington Street, just steps from the Newark Museum. The venue operates as a cabaret-style space curated by Gregory Burrus Productions, bringing world-class jazz to an intimate downtown setting.The jam sessions feature a professional house band directed by pianist and bandleader James Austin Jr., providing the kind of solid musical foundation that allows horn players, vocalists, and instrumentalists to truly stretch out. The vibe honors Newark's deep jazz heritage (Sarah Vaughan, Wayne Shorter, James Moody) while remaining accessible to developing players.PerformancesAll novice and seasoned jazz musicians and singers are welcome to jam and improvise with the professional band throughout the night. The sessions run from 7:30 PM and create space for both serious jazz study and pure enjoyment of the music. With a full bar and an atmosphere that evokes classic jazz club intimacy, Clement's Place offers what many jam sessions can't: professional-grade backline, knowledgeable audiences, and a venue designed specifically for jazz listening.Registration is required but admission remains free, democratizing access to one of the region's finest jazz environments. These sessions move fast—bring your chops, your ears, and your willingness to engage with Newark's living jazz tradition.","40.744316249704|-74.170286539145||40.744316249704, -74.170286539145","James Austin Jr.",,"In Person",,140|node|a1e41436-44fb-4b94-a82c-e8f0db8f5655|/clements-place,"Clement's Place",
137,8ef32abe-efc0-4f44-9515-44f3617b3087,149,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-01-26T23:22:57+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Evolution Dopen Mic @ NJPAC Center","2026-01-26T23:18:57+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-17T21:55:30+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Evolution Dopen Mic @ NJPAC Center | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/open-mic-njpac",/open-mic-njpac|107|en,,,"Satuday Monthly","Contact venue to confirm date",,"24 Rector St, Newark, NJ 07102","7:00 PM - 9:30 PM","Evolution Dopen Mic - NJPAC Center for Arts EducationEvolution Dopen Mic stands as one of Newark's longest-running active open mic events, born from necessity in 2014 when poet and author Sean Battle recognized the city needed a free, accessible platform for artistic expression. Now held monthly at NJPAC's Center for Arts Education, Evolution has become a Newark institution.The VibeThis isn't your standard open mic—it's a full-scale production. Each event features a 10-slot open mic list for poets, singers, emcees, and other performers, plus an ""EvoluGame"" where audience members compete in lip sync battles, dance-offs, and freestyle sessions. The night culminates with performances by ""Ascended Artists""—elite craftspeople in poetry, hip hop, and R&B.Past featured artists include HBO's Def Poetry veterans, Tony Award winners, nationally recognized poets, and acclaimed R&B artists. The purple and gold storm (Evolution's signature colors) creates an atmosphere of celebration mixed with serious artistic merit. DJ The IZM provides soundscapes, and the production values reflect Sean Battle's commitment to giving artists an experience beyond a simple open mic list.PerformancesThe $10 ticket price (reduced from earlier $5 pricing to sustain quality post-pandemic) includes snacks and beverages, with hot food available for purchase from local vendors. This is hip hop culture meeting poetry culture meeting community celebration. Sign-ups happen first-come, first-served at the door, and performers email music tracks ahead of time for seamless production.Evolution operates under the philosophy that this is ""more than a show: it is a home, with fellow artists and art lovers to learn from."" Over its decade-long run through various Newark venues (Coffee Cave, Burger Walla, Gallery 211, Mocha Lounge, Express Newark, Cryout Cave), Evolution has maintained its mission: holding space for artists to connect, form community, and express themselves.|basic_html|Evolution Dopen Mic - NJPAC Center for Arts EducationEvolution Dopen Mic stands as one of Newark's longest-running active open mic events, born from necessity in 2014 when poet and author Sean Battle recognized the city needed a free, accessible platform for artistic expression. Now held monthly at NJPAC's Center for Arts Education, Evolution has become a Newark institution.The VibeThis isn't your standard open mic—it's a full-scale production. Each event features a 10-slot open mic list for poets, singers, emcees, and other performers, plus an ""EvoluGame"" where audience members compete in lip sync battles, dance-offs, and freestyle sessions. The night culminates with performances by ""Ascended Artists""—elite craftspeople in poetry, hip hop, and R&B.Past featured artists include HBO's Def Poetry veterans, Tony Award winners, nationally recognized poets, and acclaimed R&B artists. The purple and gold storm (Evolution's signature colors) creates an atmosphere of celebration mixed with serious artistic merit. DJ The IZM provides soundscapes, and the production values reflect Sean Battle's commitment to giving artists an experience beyond a simple open mic list.PerformancesThe $10 ticket price (reduced from earlier $5 pricing to sustain quality post-pandemic) includes snacks and beverages, with hot food available for purchase from local vendors. This is hip hop culture meeting poetry culture meeting community celebration. Sign-ups happen first-come, first-served at the door, and performers email music tracks ahead of time for seamless production.Evolution operates under the philosophy that this is ""more than a show: it is a home, with fellow artists and art lovers to learn from."" Over its decade-long run through various Newark venues (Coffee Cave, Burger Walla, Gallery 211, Mocha Lounge, Express Newark, Cryout Cave), Evolution has maintained its mission: holding space for artists to connect, form community, and express themselves.","40.739933502011|-74.16793214207||40.739933502011, -74.16793214207","Sean Battle",,,,139|node|ff4ec4db-682c-46e7-be7e-0c6a94776583|/njpac-center-arts-education,"NJPAC Center for Arts Education",
