119,f95324b5-4f03-4d50-95fd-c7972a4821db,131,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-01-21T00:23:50+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Open Mic @ World Cafe Live","2026-01-21T00:20:03+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-17T21:55:30+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Open Mic @ World Cafe Live | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/open-mic-world-cafe-",/open-mic-world-cafe-|90|en,,,"First Tuesday Monthly","Philly Rising Open Mic, A FREE event for all ages.",,"3025 Walnut St, Philadelphia, PA 19104","6:00 PM - 8:00 PM","Philly Rising Open Mic at World Cafe LiveThe first Tuesday of each month, World Cafe Live partners with REC Philly to present Philly Rising Open Mic—a prestigious platform where emerging artists perform in a professional venue that has hosted national acts before they became famous.Sign-ups begin at 6 PM in The Lounge upstairs, with performances starting at 8 PM and running until 11 PM. The venue provides quality sound reinforcement and a stage with excellent sight lines—this isn't a casual bar gig but a real performance opportunity in a room designed for listening.The vibe is professional yet supportive. World Cafe Live's connection to WXPN radio means performances might receive airplay beyond the immediate audience. The venue's staff actively scouts talent, inviting exceptional performers to compete in ""Cream: The Best of Philly Rising"" on first Fridays, with winners receiving studio time and opportunities to open for established acts.Performances span all genres—acoustic singer-songwriters, hip-hop artists with backing tracks, jazz musicians, rock bands, electronic producers. The diversity reflects Philadelphia's eclectic music scene, and the quality is consistently high. This isn't a beginner-friendly open mic; it's a showcase for artists ready to take their craft to the next level.The audience includes music industry professionals, dedicated fans, and fellow musicians. People came specifically for the music, creating an attentive listening environment. The room itself is beautiful—cafe-style seating for about 100, excellent acoustics, professional lighting.World Cafe Live offers full food and beverage service, with an eclectic American menu and wide drink selection. Many performers and audience members make an evening of it, arriving for dinner before settling in for hours of live music.|basic_html|Philly Rising Open Mic at World Cafe LiveThe first Tuesday of each month, World Cafe Live partners with REC Philly to present Philly Rising Open Mic—a prestigious platform where emerging artists perform in a professional venue that has hosted national acts before they became famous.Sign-ups begin at 6 PM in The Lounge upstairs, with performances starting at 8 PM and running until 11 PM. The venue provides quality sound reinforcement and a stage with excellent sight lines—this isn't a casual bar gig but a real performance opportunity in a room designed for listening.The vibe is professional yet supportive. World Cafe Live's connection to WXPN radio means performances might receive airplay beyond the immediate audience. The venue's staff actively scouts talent, inviting exceptional performers to compete in ""Cream: The Best of Philly Rising"" on first Fridays, with winners receiving studio time and opportunities to open for established acts.Performances span all genres—acoustic singer-songwriters, hip-hop artists with backing tracks, jazz musicians, rock bands, electronic producers. The diversity reflects Philadelphia's eclectic music scene, and the quality is consistently high. This isn't a beginner-friendly open mic; it's a showcase for artists ready to take their craft to the next level.The audience includes music industry professionals, dedicated fans, and fellow musicians. People came specifically for the music, creating an attentive listening environment. The room itself is beautiful—cafe-style seating for about 100, excellent acoustics, professional lighting.World Cafe Live offers full food and beverage service, with an eclectic American menu and wide drink selection. Many performers and audience members make an evening of it, arriving for dinner before settling in for hours of live music.","39.952268805664|-75.184593266122||39.952268805664, -75.184593266122","REC Philly",,"In Person",,120|node|9f1f5ef1-e8b0-4768-b2b2-4e716099ee70|/world-cafe-live-philly,"World Cafe Live",
117,b94bd198-4fa2-4c93-941e-c3f893e9740a,129,en,events|node_type|76710fc4-3157-498e-ba85-0501ed7ed1ac,"2026-01-20T23:43:20+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,,1,1|user|85298f8d-c10c-44ac-af32-f23600324c58|/user/1,"Open Mic @ Fergie's Pub","2026-01-20T23:39:56+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP","2026-02-17T21:55:30+00:00|Y-m-d\TH:i:sP",,,1,1,"meta|title|Open Mic @ Fergie's Pub | Open Jam Events|meta|robots|index, follow|link|canonical|https://openjamevents.com/open-mic-fergies-pub",/open-mic-fergies-pub|88|en,Acoustic,,Mondays,"Refreshing Vibe (NO TVs!) Come out and play, listen and engage with other human beings",,"1214 Sansom St, Philadelphia, PA 19107","8:30 PM - 11:00 PM","Poetry & Music at Fergie's PubFergie's Pub's upstairs room hosts multiple weekly events, but the Wednesday offerings showcase the venue's commitment to diverse artistic expression. At 7 PM, poets gather for the Poetry Open Mic, creating space for spoken word artists to share their work. At 8:30 PM, musicians can sign up for the Music Open Mic, which runs from 9 PM onward. And at 9:30 PM, Off Leash Comedy takes over for free stand-up showcasing some of Philly's best comics.The vibe is distinctly Irish pub—warm, welcoming, and slightly chaotic in the best way. The upstairs room is small and often crowded, creating intimacy between performers and audience. It's a listening room where people actually pay attention, not a sports bar where artists compete with televisions.The Poetry Open Mic attracts serious writers testing new work, slam poets honing performance skills, and first-timers finding courage to share their words publicly. The format is supportive and democratic—everyone gets their time, and the audience provides encouragement rather than judgment.The Music Open Mic leans acoustic—the space works better for solo artists and duos than full electric bands—but all genres are welcome. Singer-songwriters dominate, but don't be surprised to hear jazz standards, folk traditionals, or experimental compositions.Fergie's is a genuine Irish pub with Philly flair, serving excellent food (the Guinness onion soup is legendary) and pouring a proper Guinness. The staff understands the arts—they create space for performers while maintaining the pub's convivial atmosphere. It's been a Center City institution for nearly 25 years, surviving through authenticity and commitment to community.|basic_html|Poetry & Music at Fergie's PubFergie's Pub's upstairs room hosts multiple weekly events, but the Wednesday offerings showcase the venue's commitment to diverse artistic expression. At 7 PM, poets gather for the Poetry Open Mic, creating space for spoken word artists to share their work. At 8:30 PM, musicians can sign up for the Music Open Mic, which runs from 9 PM onward. And at 9:30 PM, Off Leash Comedy takes over for free stand-up showcasing some of Philly's best comics.The vibe is distinctly Irish pub—warm, welcoming, and slightly chaotic in the best way. The upstairs room is small and often crowded, creating intimacy between performers and audience. It's a listening room where people actually pay attention, not a sports bar where artists compete with televisions.The Poetry Open Mic attracts serious writers testing new work, slam poets honing performance skills, and first-timers finding courage to share their words publicly. The format is supportive and democratic—everyone gets their time, and the audience provides encouragement rather than judgment.The Music Open Mic leans acoustic—the space works better for solo artists and duos than full electric bands—but all genres are welcome. Singer-songwriters dominate, but don't be surprised to hear jazz standards, folk traditionals, or experimental compositions.Fergie's is a genuine Irish pub with Philly flair, serving excellent food (the Guinness onion soup is legendary) and pouring a proper Guinness. The staff understands the arts—they create space for performers while maintaining the pub's convivial atmosphere. It's been a Center City institution for nearly 25 years, surviving through authenticity and commitment to community.","39.949825358277|-75.16074281772||39.949825358277, -75.16074281772",,,,,,"Fergie's Pub",
